#
# Milestone M5 of the Racket reference engine: 9 conformance case(s).
#
# Tate-chu-yoko.
#
# One case identifier per line, in the order `jlreq-conformance list` prints
# them. A `#` line and a blank line are comments. The nine files partition the
# eighty-nine built-in cases: every case is in exactly one of them, so the
# cumulative suite M1..Mn grows monotonically and M1..M9 is the whole suite.
#
# M5 is complete when the cumulative suite through M5 runs green:
#
#   cat engines/racket/milestones/M{1..5}.ids | ...select from suite.ndjson...
#   cargo run -p jlreq-conformance -- run ENGINE PARTIAL.ndjson   # exit 0

